classDiagram
    %% PawPal+ UML, revised after the skeleton review (see reflection.md section 1b).
    %% Keep this file updated so it matches your final implementation.

    class Owner {
        +str name
        +int available_minutes
        +list~str~ preferences
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet: Pet) None
        +set_available_time(minutes: int) None
        +update_preferences(preferences: list~str~) None
        +get_all_tasks() list~Task~
    }

    class Pet {
        +str name
        +str species
        +str breed
        +int age
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task: Task) None
        +remove_task(task_id: str) None
        +get_tasks() list~Task~
    }

    class Task {
        +str title
        +int duration_minutes
        +str priority
        +str category
        +str preferred_time
        +str frequency
        +date last_completed
        +str pet_name
        +str task_id
        +priority_rank() int
        +edit(title: str, duration_minutes: int, priority: str) None
        +mark_complete(on: date) None
        +is_due(on: date) bool
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +list~Task~ scheduled_tasks
        +list~Task~ skipped_tasks
        +generate_plan(on: date) list~Task~
        +explain_plan() str
    }

    note for Task "priority: high | medium | low, ranked 3 / 2 / 1 via PRIORITY_RANK\nfrequency: daily | weekly"

    Owner "1" o-- "0..*" Pet : has
    Pet "1" *-- "0..*" Task : has
    Task ..> Pet : belongs to (pet_name)
    Scheduler --> Owner : uses time and all pets' tasks
    Scheduler --> Task : schedules or skips
